From cc630a30df060dc52736342be1ba583639d8a7f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 04:12:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(webdriverio): keep a multi-remote test running when one
 instance closes its last window

Closing the last window of a browser ends its WebDriver session, and the
context manager then threw "All window handles were removed, causing
WebdriverIO to close the session." from the closeWindow result. In a
multi-remote browser each instance is its own session, so closing the only
window of one instance made closeWindow() reject and ended the test while
the other instances were still open.

MultiRemote.addInstance now marks each instance browser, and the context
manager no longer throws for a marked browser: it clears the cached context
and window handle, logs a warning that the session of that instance ended,
and lets an error of the closeWindow command itself reach the caller
unchanged. The mark lives in a WeakSet keyed by the browser object, so it is
kept when the session manager is recreated after reloadSession(). A browser
that is not part of a multi-remote browser still gets the error.

Fix #15043
